WEBVTT

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.120
Folks, as many of you know, we're having trouble passing the budget this year.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.1000
Because the town's emergency reserve fund is only 10% of the budget,

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.535
Andover can't just delay sending out the tax bills or we risk running out of money.

00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:26.575
The Board of Selectmen set a mill rate at a June 24 special meeting based on their best estimate of what the final town budget will be.

00:00:26.895 --> 00:00:29.375
This allows the tax bills to go out on time.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:33.430
They chose to set the mill rate at 36,

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.350
which is 0.39

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.750
mills higher than the current mill rate.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:47.165
If the budget that is eventually approved is higher or lower than what the Board of Select and set, the town may need to send out a correction later.

00:00:48.045 --> 00:00:50.925
Tax bills will be going out in the next few days.

00:00:51.405 --> 00:00:54.925
The first installment is due on 07/01/2021.

00:00:55.405 --> 00:01:01.680
Payments must be postmarked, paid online, or brought to the town hall by 08/02/2021

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.600
to avoid an interest charge.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.880
Thank you for your patience during a difficult budget process.
